<title>SWEDEN: Sweden-ERM more likely as economy stable-Riksbank.</title>
<headline>Sweden-ERM more likely as economy stable-Riksbank.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Urban Backstrom, governor of Sweden's Riksbank, on Thursday said linking the crown to the EU's Exchange Rate Mechanism (ERM) becomes more possible as the country's economy continues to stabilise.  </p>
<p>&quot;As (economic) growth continues more thoroughly, with increased stability, there is more of a possibility of the ERM question,&quot; Backstrom told a question and answer session after a finance committee hearing.</p>
<p>But he said there needed to be board support for Sweden to link the crown to the ERM before it went ahead.</p>
<p>&quot;All the economic policies and even the public ought to stand behind the decision,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>&quot;It is natural that the question of a common currency be treated as a common interest.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
